user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 25,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_has_personal_anecdote",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text (post body): 1 if it includes a personal anecdote or first-person experiential narrative about the OP's own experiences, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP post body; may contain later edits, which cannot be separated, so judge the text as given). Return 1 if the OP recounts a personal anecdote or first-person experiential narrative about events or experiences they themselves lived (e.g., 'when I worked at...', 'my friend and I experienced...' as lived by OP). Return 0 if the text contains only abstract claims, hypotheticals, general statistics, or others' experiences with no OP personal experience. Exclude quoted external text, and mere opinion statements like 'I think' without an experience. Null if argument is missing or unparseable; empty text gives null."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 62,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_argument_has_personal_anecdote",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text: 1 if it contains at least one direct personal anecdote told by the OP (a specific experience that happened to the OP), else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP's post body). Return 1 if the OP, in their own voice, recounts at least one direct personal anecdote: a specific first-person experience or event that happened to the OP (e.g. 'when I worked at X, my boss...', 'I once got denied...'). Experiences of the OP's close family or friends do not count unless the OP also narrates their own involvement. Return 0 if there is none: only abstract reasoning, generic claims, hypotheticals, statistics, third-party or news examples, general statements of opinion or identity without a specific experience, or merely stating a view held ('I believe'). Exclude text inside quotation or block-quote markers that quotes others, and exclude edit notes/responses added after the original text (marked EDIT/Edit/Update). If argument is missing, empty or unparseable return null. Output 1, 0 or null."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 79,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_has_personal_experience_narrative",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text: 1 if it contains an explicit narrative of the OP's own personal experience (events that happened to or were done by the OP), else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP's post body). Return 1 if the OP, in their own voice, explicitly recounts a personal experience narrative: specific first-person events, situations or episodes they lived through or did (e.g. 'when I worked at X, I saw...', 'my sister and I ...'). Return 0 if the argument contains only abstract claims, general reasoning, hypotheticals, third-party or hearsay examples, or opinions without a recounted personal experience; also 0 for passing mentions of identity or a bare stance ('I think', 'I am a student') with no experience recounted. Exclude text inside quotations of other people and moderator/bot notices or edit notes not narrating the OP's experience. Do not use title, comments or conversation. Empty or missing argument: null."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
